Z||000000||npavlo||09-16-2000||07:00 PM||||first of all. thanks for all the input i recieved in my previous questions.. it helped ALOT....  NOW...<P>the muncies ive seen seem to be designed rather clunky and not good..  like the fifth gear add on the end of it under the side cover... it looks just weaker to me.. but hey ifyou guys run it.. hell..  but now another question..<P>the isuzu transes ive seen have the wimpiest axles.. are the muncie and isuzu axles the same fit and splines?  or if you were to put a isuzu trans in a fiero will 4 cyliner axles be needed (if theyre different)?  if theyre the same... ****  my getrag 284 (3.4L DOHC FWD transaxle, rarest of them all) has practiacally double the size shafts..  how thick rougly are the axles in fieros with muncies?  my axles are about 1 in thich roubly.. the isuzu i saw were MAYBE 3/4" if lucky... <P>main question..<P>are the axles interchangeble in between muncie (getrag fiero) and isuzu?  or do you go with the isuzu axles from the 4 cylinders (if theyre different)?   also how thick are they roughly?<P><P>------------------<BR>1991 Cutlass Supreme International 3.4L DOHC<BR>5-Speed Getrag 284<BR>Blown Trans, possibly going into fiero --||||reg||5
Z||000001||pherder||09-16-2000||07:30 PM||||The axles are the same (actually it is the CVs that are the same since that is what plugs into the transaxle ...)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>I have both and have swapped axles between the two.<P>BTW, Archie used to tell anyone that got his V8 kit that if you broke a stock axle he would come out to your place and change it for you.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||09-16-2000||08:12 PM|||| I also beleive that both types of trans' use the same axles. I don't think they will ever break. I used 4 cyl axles with a 350 TPI with never a problem. <P>I remember reading about someone who kept breaking axles, or was that the twin turbo 2.8 tale teller? (read that 10 times fast!)<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)||||reg||1
Z||000003||henrik||09-20-2000||03:04 PM||||I recently replaced my L4+Izuzu 5sp with a v6+getrag 5sp and I kept the axles, they´re the same.<BR>/ Henrik ||||reg||1
